# craigslist-scraper — credentials and defaults
#
# Copy this file to `.env` next to the scripts and fill in what you use:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is in .gitignore. Keep it there. A secret passed on a command line
# is readable by anything that can run `ps` and lands in your shell history,
# which is why none of these has a flag you are expected to type.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#
#     explicit CLI flag  >  exported environment variable  >  .env  >  default
#
# So a `.env` never overrides something you typed, and an already-exported
# variable (a CI secret, direnv, your shell profile) is never clobbered by a
# file you forgot to delete.
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing any secret:
#
#     python3 env_config.py
#
# Every variable below is one this code actually reads, and every variable
# the code reads is below — smoke_test.py asserts the two sets are equal in
# both directions, because a documented-but-unread variable is worse than an
# undocumented one.
#
# Copying this file and running WITHOUT editing it is also a tested path: the
# loader treats every credential here as unset, so you get a clear "not
# configured" rather than a 401 a long way from its cause. Only
# CRAIGSLIST_URL below is meant to work as it stands.


# --- 2Captcha -------------------------------------------------------------
# One key, four separately-billed products: captcha solving, the Scraping
# Browser API, proxies and fingerprints. https://2captcha.com
#
# WORTH KNOWING BEFORE YOU BUY SOLVING FOR THIS SITE: no challenge of any
# kind has been observed on the pages this scraper reads. Measured 2026-09-14
# across 22 captures covering six categories and five locales — zero
# reCAPTCHA, hCaptcha, Turnstile, DataDome, PerimeterX, Incapsula, Akamai or
# AWS WAF markers, no challenge iframe, no data-sitekey, and the word
# "captcha" itself appears zero times on any of them.
#
# What Craigslist does to an address it has scored has NOT been measured
# here, because nothing this repo ran was refused — including from a
# datacentre address in Germany, which returned the full listing. So this
# file does not claim to know, and the scraper decides "blocked" structurally
# (was this page built out of the site's own assets?) rather than by hunting
# for a vendor's marker.
#
# The solving path is wired up and capped at one purchase per page, because a
# bot manager can be switched on between deploys and a scraper that cannot
# name what stopped it is much harder to fix. It is not part of the happy
# path.
#
# This key IS what --fingerprint uses (a separate subscription from solving:
# a working solver key is not automatically enabled for fingerprints, and the
# client says so by name if it is not).
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# --- Scraping Browser API -------------------------------------------------
# A remote browser you do not run or patch, with a persistent profile and a
# chosen exit country. Used by --cdp-endpoint.
#
#   country-  picks the exit country. On this site it decides ACCESS and
#             nothing about the content: the currency and language follow the
#             AREA in the URL, measured 2026-09-14 by fetching eight areas
#             through one US exit and getting USD, CAD, EUR, JPY and MXN
#             back. There is no --country flag on the scrapers for the same
#             reason.
#   pid-      is a profile with persistent cookies. ONE live connection each,
#             capped per account — reuse pids rather than minting one per
#             run, and expect a connect timeout (exit 5, "profile_locked")
#             while another run still holds this one. Measured: two runs
#             launched back to back against one pid, the second exited 5.
#             Leave roughly a minute between runs on one pid, and give CI its
#             own.
#
# Two things measured on this endpoint that are worth knowing:
#
#   The profile keeps COOKIES, not an address. Three connections to one pid
#   gave three different exits (NJ/Cablevision, NC/NorthState, …), while
#   within a single held connection the exit was stable for the full eight
#   minutes sampled. So a run never rotates under itself; consecutive runs on
#   one pid replay one profile's cookies from different addresses.
#
#   Over this endpoint the Playwright and Selenium engines cannot switch
#   JavaScript off, so they read the site's rendered grid rather than its
#   served list — about 200 rows with no coordinates, against ~350 with them.
#   puppeteer_scraper.py CAN (it sets it per page) and is the better choice
#   for a single-batch run over a remote profile.
#
# Note that Selenium cannot use this at all: chromedriver's `debuggerAddress`
# takes a bare host:port with nowhere to put a password. Playwright and
# pyppeteer authenticate on the WebSocket upgrade and work.
# selenium_scraper.py refuses a credentialed endpoint with exit 2 and says
# which engine to use instead.
CRAIGSLIST_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-us-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# --- Proxy ----------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT required to reach this site, which is unusual in this family and worth
# saying plainly: measured 2026-09-14, a datacentre address in Germany was
# served the full New York listing — 536,962 bytes, 296 results — with no
# proxy, no key and no challenge.
#
# What a proxy buys here is the exit COUNTRY, volume from many addresses, and
# somewhere to go if an address is ever scored.
#
# USE THE socks5 PORT. Measured on the 2Captcha residential gateway: socks5
# on :2333 works, and the http form on :2334 timed out twice at 40s and 45s.
# The rest of this family documents the http form; for this credential it is
# dead.
#
# The `session-` token is arbitrary — you choose it, and a different token is
# a different exit. Four invented tokens returned four distinct US residential
# exits (Arizona/Wyyerd, Kansas/AT&T, Texas/AT&T, Maine/Charter), so ONE login
# is a pool: --proxy-file with one line per session token needs no extra
# credentials.
#
# `sessTime-` is how long that exit is held, in minutes, and LONGER is right.
# A rotation is supposed to be a fresh browser; a sticky window expiring
# mid-run changes the exit UNDER a live session, at a moment you did not
# choose. 30 was verified to hold: sampled every 60s for 600s, the same
# address at every point, including past the 5-minute mark.
#
# The credentials here never reach the browser's command line — they go
# through the driver's own fields. Logs keep the host and port and mask the
# rest, because which exit a run used is the point of the log and is not the
# secret. Selenium's --proxy-server cannot authenticate at all, so that engine
# strips the credentials and warns rather than letting you believe a
# user:pass URL is doing something.
CRAIGSLIST_PROXY=socks5://{user}-zone-custom-region-us-session-{sessionId}-sessTime-30:{password}@na.proxy.2captcha.com:2333

# --- Default target -------------------------------------------------------
# Saves retyping --url. Craigslist has ONE hostname worldwide and the area is
# a path segment — its own index lists 714 of them — so there is no
# per-country host to get wrong and no locale prefix.
#
#   /search/area/{slug}?cat={code}      a result list for a whole area
#   /search/subarea/{slug}?cat={code}   one subarea of it
#   /view/d/{slug}/{token}              one advert, with --mode posting
#   /area/{slug}                        an area LANDING page, which has no
#                                       results of its own: 0 rows, exit 4
#
# There are no pages: `?page=` and `?s=` return the same document byte for
# byte, so --pages walks the rendered list instead, and one URL tops out at
# 10,000 results however far it is walked. Past that, narrow the URL with the
# site's own filters — &min_price=/&max_price=, &query=, &postedToday=1,
# &hasPic=1, or a subarea — and run each separately. All of them are real
# server-side parameters; measured, each returns a different result set.
CRAIGSLIST_URL=https://www.craigslist.org/search/area/newyork?cat=sss

# Deliberately NOT here: an output prefix. `--out` already carries a
# non-empty default, so the loader — which only fills UNSET values — would
# never see it, and the variable would be silently inert: a setting that
# looks configurable and is not.
